<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gongyang of Goryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1345–1394</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gongyang was the last king of Goryeo, reigning from 1389 to 1392. Placed on the throne by the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-joseon">Yi Seong-gye</a> and his allies, he had little real power, and after the killing of the loyalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeong-mong-ju">Jeong Mong-ju</a> in 1392 he was deposed and Yi founded the Joseon dynasty. He was later sent into exile and killed in 1394.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gongyang-of-goryeo.jpg" alt="Gongyang of Goryeo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: QWMN1409 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EA%B3%A0%EC%96%91_%EA%B3%B5%EC%96%91%EC%99%95%EB%A6%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
